---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="DecayFix terms of service regarding report purchases and tool usage."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-20">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white mb-8">Terms of Service</h1>
    
    <div class="prose prose-invert prose-slate max-w-none text-slate-300 space-y-6 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-slate-400">Last updated: September 12, 2026</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing DecayFix and connecting your Google Search Console account, you agree to these Terms of Service.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">2. Service Scope</h2>
      <p>
        DecayFix is an analytical tool providing traffic decay diagnostics and AI-generated editorial suggestions. While our suggestions are tailored to content freshness best practices, we cannot guarantee specific ranking or traffic increases from Google Search algorithm changes.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">3. Purchases & 7-Day Refund Guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        DecayFix Full Site Unlocks are backed by our <strong>7-Day Money-Back Guarantee</strong>. If our content decay diagnostics and AI action plans do not uncover actionable traffic recovery opportunities for your website, simply email support@decayfix.com within 7 days of purchase for a 100% full refund, no questions asked.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">4. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        DecayFix is provided "as is" without warranty of any kind. We are not liable for changes in website rankings, search penalties, or lost revenue resulting from editorial actions taken on your blog.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
